  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Arpraziquantel is the (R)-enantiomer of the anthelmintic praziquantel, developed for treating schistosomiasis and other trematode worm infections. It remains investigational and is not an authorised medicine; the established praziquantel is widely used, mainly in tropical regions.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27292599&quot;>Wikidata Q27292599</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>arpraziquantel</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>P02BA03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11749&quot;>DB11749</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/445900&quot;>445900</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27292599&quot;>Q27292599</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C19H24N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>312.413 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
